{
  "rationale": "The plant models robot motion and perception as separate automata. The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are used only when obstacles are detected. Recovery is conservative but returns to exploration as soon as the path is clear. Full_rotate is reserved for repeated or dead-end obstacles. All transitions are deterministic and respect the event and state constraints.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion commands and sensor outcomes to clarify controllable/uncontrollable event flow.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe exploration: random_walk in clear, move_forward for short progress, rotate recovery on obstacles, and quick return to exploration after path_clear."
  ],
